/* Deep interpretations: Sun, Moon, Mercury, Venus, Mars and Jupiter through the twelve houses */
window.AstroDeep = window.AstroDeep || {};
window.AstroDeep.planetHouses1 = {
  sun: {
    1: {
      text: "With the Sun in the first house, your identity is on display before you say a word. People notice you arrive, and you tend to lead with your whole self: your body, your appearance and your way of starting things all carry a strong sense of who you are. This gives you natural presence and the courage to go first. The difficulty is that you can take everything personally, since so much of your energy is tied to how you come across. Feedback about your approach can feel like a verdict on your worth. You grow most when you let your vitality serve something beyond your own reflection, and when you allow others the same visibility you enjoy.",
      advice: "Start one thing each month purely because it expresses you, and notice when you need an audience before you can feel sure of yourself."
    },
    2: {
      text: "Your sense of self is tied closely to what you can build, earn and hold. The second house Sun wants tangible proof of value, so you often feel most like yourself when your talents are producing something real, whether that is income, a well-made object or a skill honed over years. You tend to be steady, loyal to what you own and slow to part with it. The shadow side is measuring your worth by your bank balance or possessions, which can make lean periods feel like personal failure. Your deeper task is to recognise the worth that exists in you before it is converted into money, and to spend in line with your actual values.",
      advice: "Write down three talents you would keep practising even if nobody paid you, and give at least one of them regular time each week."
    },
    3: {
      text: "Here the Sun shines on words, ideas and the everyday traffic of life. You come alive in conversation, in learning something new and in moving around your local area, and you may be known for your curiosity or your way with language. Siblings, cousins or close neighbours often play a formative role, as rivals, allies or mirrors. Writing, teaching, sales, media and any work that links people to information suit you well. The trouble is restlessness: you can scatter your light across too many interests, or feel invisible when nobody is listening. Depth comes when you choose a few subjects and let your mind stay with them long enough to say something of your own.",
      advice: "Keep a notebook for one subject you care about and add to it daily until your own point of view becomes clear."
    },
    4: {
      text: "The fourth house Sun puts your centre of gravity at home. Your identity grows from roots: family history, the place you come from and the private life you build behind closed doors. You may be the emotional anchor of your family, or you may spend years working out who you are apart from a strong parent, often the father. Public recognition tends to matter less than feeling secure, and many people with this placement come into their own later in life, once the home base is settled. The challenge is hiding too long in familiar rooms, or letting old family patterns define you. A home that reflects who you are now becomes your quiet source of strength.",
      advice: "Make one change to your living space this season that reflects the person you are now, rather than the family you came from."
    },
    5: {
      text: "Few placements are as naturally expressive. With the Sun in the fifth house, you need to create, play and be seen enjoying yourself, and life feels flat without some outlet for self-expression. This might be performance, art, sport, games, flirting or raising children, and many people with this placement have a strong bond with kids or a lasting youthful streak. Romance matters, and you tend to love with warmth and generosity. The risk is depending on applause, taking gambles to feel alive, or sulking when your efforts go unnoticed. Your greatest gift appears when you create for the sheer pleasure of it and let your delight spill over to the people around you.",
      advice: "Set aside a regular block of time for making something purely for enjoyment, with no plan to share or sell the result."
    },
    6: {
      text: "You find your sense of purpose in useful work and the rhythm of daily life. The sixth house Sun likes to be good at things, to improve systems and to be the person others rely on, and you often shine as a skilled practitioner, a problem-solver or someone in a helping role. Health and routine are closely linked to your vitality, so how you eat, sleep and move tends to show quickly in your mood. The difficulty is over-identifying with productivity, feeling worthless on rest days or carrying colleagues' workloads without credit. Pets and small daily rituals can be surprisingly nourishing. You thrive when your work is valued and your body is treated as a partner.",
      advice: "Build one non-negotiable rest period into your week and treat it with the same seriousness you give your work commitments."
    },
    7: {
      text: "Your identity tends to come into focus through other people. With the Sun in the seventh house, partnerships of every kind, from marriage to business alliances, are where you learn who you are. You often have a gift for diplomacy, for seeing both sides and for bringing out the best in a partner. You may be drawn to strong, confident people who carry qualities you have yet to claim for yourself. The difficulty is defining yourself by your relationship status or deferring so much that you lose your own direction. Open conflicts can also be clarifying for you. Real partnership arrives when two whole people meet, each keeping their own light.",
      advice: "Before agreeing to a shared plan, pause and ask what you would choose if you were deciding entirely on your own."
    },
    8: {
      text: "The eighth house Sun draws you toward what lies under the surface. You tend to be private, perceptive and interested in the hidden workings of people, money and power. Intimacy is a serious matter for you, and you may find that close relationships change you profoundly. Shared resources, inheritance, investments or other people's money can feature strongly in your life or work. Periods of crisis often mark turning points, and you can emerge from loss with more strength than before. The shadow is a pull toward control, secrecy or intensity for its own sake. Your light grows when you trust others with your vulnerability as much as with your strength.",
      advice: "Choose one person you trust and share something real about yourself that you would usually keep behind a guarded front."
    },
    9: {
      text: "You feel most alive when your horizons are expanding. With the Sun in the ninth house, travel, study, faith and big questions about meaning are central to who you are. You may be drawn to university life, teaching, publishing, law or living abroad, and many people with this placement feel their true self emerges far from home. You have a natural enthusiasm for ideas and can inspire others with your vision. The pitfall is preaching, restlessness or chasing the next adventure to avoid the ordinary work of the present. Your beliefs gain weight when you test them in real life and stay open to views that challenge them.",
      advice: "Pick one belief you hold strongly and seek out a thoughtful source that disagrees, then read it with genuine curiosity."
    },
    10: {
      text: "Here the Sun sits at the top of the chart, and your life often has a public dimension. Career, reputation and what you achieve in the world are closely tied to your sense of self. You tend to be ambitious, capable of leadership and willing to take responsibility, and others may see you as an authority even before you feel like one. A parent, often the one who shaped your expectations, may loom large in your drive to succeed. The difficulty is equating worth with status, or feeling lost between goals. Your standing becomes far more satisfying when the work itself genuinely expresses who you are and what you care about.",
      advice: "Review your career goals once a year and cross out any that belong to someone else's expectations rather than your own."
    },
    11: {
      text: "Your sense of self grows through friendship, community and shared ideals. The eleventh house Sun often makes you a connector, the person who brings a group together or champions a cause larger than yourself. You tend to feel most alive working toward a future you believe in, whether through activism, professional networks, clubs or online communities. Friends may matter to you as much as family. The trouble comes when you lose your individuality in the group or keep people at a friendly distance to avoid deeper intimacy. Your hopes are a real guide here, and naming them clearly helps you find the people who share them.",
      advice: "Write down one hope for the next five years and tell a friend, so it becomes something you work toward together."
    },
    12: {
      text: "The Sun in the twelfth house often gives a quieter, more inward kind of identity. You may feel most yourself when alone, in nature, in meditation or in creative states where time falls away. Many people with this placement work behind the scenes, in healing, research, hospitals, retreats or the arts, and they tend to be deeply compassionate. Recognition can feel uncomfortable, and you may downplay your gifts or feel unsure who you are. The challenge is self-undoing through avoidance, overgiving or losing yourself in escapism. Solitude is a genuine need here, and when honoured, it becomes the source from which your confidence and sense of direction slowly grow.",
      advice: "Protect a daily window of solitude, even fifteen minutes, and use it to listen inwardly before the demands of the day begin."
    }
  },

  moon: {
    1: {
      text: "Your feelings tend to show on your face. With the Moon in the first house, emotions shape your appearance, your first impressions and the way you approach anything new, so people often read your mood before you have named it. You come across as approachable, responsive and caring, and others may confide in you quickly. Your body is sensitive to your emotional state, and your energy can rise and fall with the tides of your inner life. The difficulty is being so porous that other people's moods become yours. Learning to notice what you feel, and choosing when to share it, gives you both warmth and steadiness.",
      advice: "When you walk into a room, take one breath to check your own mood before responding to the atmosphere around you."
    },
    2: {
      text: "Emotional security and material security are bound together for you. The Moon in the second house tends to feel safest with a full pantry, savings in the bank and familiar things around you, and your possessions often carry strong sentimental meaning. Your income may fluctuate, rising and falling in cycles, and you might earn through food, care, property, hospitality or anything that nourishes people. You have a real gift for creating comfort. The challenge is comfort buying, hoarding or feeling anxious whenever money is uncertain. Your worth is steadier than your finances, and building a small safety buffer can calm a lot of old worry.",
      advice: "Notice when you shop to soothe a feeling, and try naming the feeling first before deciding whether you still want the purchase."
    },
    3: {
      text: "Your mind and your emotions are closely linked, so you often process feelings by talking, writing or messaging. The third house Moon tends to make you chatty, curious and sensitive to tone, and you may remember conversations more for how they felt than for what was said. Siblings or close neighbours may have played a nurturing role, or your emotional life at home may have been shaped by a brother or sister. Short trips and familiar local routes can settle you. The downside is a restless, worried mind that replays exchanges late at night. Journalling or talking things through with one trusted person helps turn busy thinking into understanding.",
      advice: "Before bed, write a few lines about what you felt today so your mind can let the day's conversations go."
    },
    4: {
      text: "This is the Moon's natural home, and your emotional life is deeply rooted in family, home and the past. You often need a safe, private nest where you can retreat and recharge, and you may be the one who keeps traditions, recipes and memories alive. Your relationship with your mother or main caregiver is likely to be central, whether close, complicated or both. Property, gardening, cooking and anything domestic can be satisfying. The difficulty is getting stuck in old moods, clinging to the familiar or feeling unsettled whenever home is disrupted. As you age, your inner world often becomes richer, and a home you have shaped yourself brings real contentment.",
      advice: "Create one small ritual at home, such as a weekly shared meal, that makes your space feel like a genuine sanctuary."
    },
    5: {
      text: "Your feelings want to be expressed, played with and shared. With the Moon in the fifth house, creativity, romance and fun are emotional necessities, and you may feel low when there is no outlet for joy. Many people with this placement have a strong instinct for nurturing children or a childlike spontaneity of their own. You tend to fall in love with your whole heart and can be tender, dramatic and generous in romance. Things get harder when you need constant reassurance, or when your moods swing with the reception of your creative projects. Play is genuinely healing for you, so treating it as a priority helps keep your emotional balance.",
      advice: "Schedule something playful each week, like dancing, painting or a game with friends, and treat it as essential emotional care."
    },
    6: {
      text: "You find emotional comfort in routine, usefulness and caring for others in practical ways. The sixth house Moon often shows up as the colleague who remembers birthdays, the friend who brings soup, or the person who feels calmer after cleaning the kitchen. Work environments matter to your mood, and a tense workplace can affect you physically. Your digestion and energy levels may be closely tied to stress. Pets can be deeply soothing. The harder side is fretting over small details or caring for everyone else while neglecting your own needs. A gentle daily rhythm that includes rest, good food and movement tends to keep you steady.",
      advice: "Pay attention to what your body tells you after a stressful workday, and adjust your routines before tiredness builds up."
    },
    7: {
      text: "You tend to feel emotionally complete when you are in close partnership. The seventh house Moon seeks a partner who offers comfort and understanding, and you are often attuned to what others need, sometimes before they know it themselves. Relationships may carry echoes of your early bond with your mother, so you might find yourself mothering a partner or hoping to be mothered. Your public dealings, contracts and collaborations can be coloured by your moods. The challenge is dependence, or losing touch with your own feelings while tracking someone else's. Emotional honesty with a partner, including naming your own needs, makes intimacy feel safer on both sides.",
      advice: "In your closest relationship, practise naming one of your own needs each week, clearly and without apology."
    },
    8: {
      text: "Your emotions run deep and are rarely on the surface. With the Moon in the eighth house, you tend to feel things intensely and privately, sensing undercurrents in people and situations that others miss. Intimacy is where you feel most alive and most exposed, so trust is earned slowly. Shared finances, inheritance or family money may carry strong emotional charge. You may have experienced loss or upheaval early, which can give you real resilience and a gift for supporting others through crisis. The difficulty is holding onto hurt, fearing abandonment or trying to control people to feel safe. Psychological work and honest conversation can be deeply healing here.",
      advice: "When a strong feeling surfaces, give it a name out loud to someone you trust before deciding what to do with it."
    },
    9: {
      text: "You feel at home in the world of ideas, beliefs and distant places. The ninth house Moon often finds emotional comfort in philosophy, spirituality, study or travel, and you may feel restless when life becomes too small. Your family may have had strong religious or cultural beliefs that shaped you, whether you kept them or moved away from them. Living abroad, or feeling oddly at home in another culture, is common. You tend to be emotionally generous and optimistic. The challenge is using big ideas or constant movement to avoid facing ordinary feelings. When your beliefs are grounded in lived experience, they become a real source of comfort.",
      advice: "Take a short trip or course when you feel stuck, then reflect on what it taught you about your needs at home."
    },
    10: {
      text: "Your emotional life has a public side, and people often know how you feel. With the Moon in the tenth house, your career tends to involve care, the public or anything that responds to people's needs, such as health, hospitality, education or property. You may be well liked and seen as approachable in your professional role. A parent, often the mother, may have been influential in your ambitions. Your reputation can rise and fall with public mood, and criticism may leave you feeling exposed. The trap is needing your work to meet all your emotional needs. Building a private life separate from your role helps you feel secure.",
      advice: "Keep at least one area of your life, such as a hobby or friendship, entirely separate from your professional identity."
    },
    11: {
      text: "Friendship is where you feel most at home. The eleventh house Moon tends to make your friends feel like family, and you often take a caring role within groups, clubs or communities. You may be drawn to causes that protect or nurture people, and you can sense the mood of a crowd easily. Your hopes for the future carry strong feeling, and your goals may shift as your emotional needs change. The difficulty is depending too much on group approval, or feeling lonely even when surrounded by acquaintances. A few deep friendships, more than many light ones, usually give you the belonging you seek.",
      advice: "Invest time in two or three friendships that feel truly nourishing, and let some of the more draining social commitments fall away."
    },
    12: {
      text: "Much of your emotional life happens behind closed doors. With the Moon in the twelfth house, you may feel things deeply but struggle to express them, or you might absorb other people's feelings without realising. Solitude, dreams and quiet reflection are essential for recharging, and you may have a strong intuitive or spiritual sensitivity. Many people with this placement are drawn to caring roles in hospitals, retreats or charities. There may be unspoken emotions in your family history that shape you. The risk is withdrawal, escapism or a sense of being unseen. Gently bringing your inner world into the light, through creativity or trusted company, can be very healing.",
      advice: "Keep a dream journal by your bed and note recurring images, as they often point to feelings you have yet to express."
    }
  },

  mercury: {
    1: {
      text: "Your mind is part of your first impression. With Mercury in the first house, you tend to come across as quick, alert and talkative, and people may notice your wit, curiosity or restless energy straight away. You approach life by asking questions, making connections and thinking on your feet. You may look youthful or move with a lively, nervous energy. Communication is central to how you define yourself, so writing, speaking or teaching can be natural strengths. The flip side is overthinking, interrupting or talking yourself into anxiety. Slowing down enough to listen, as well as to speak, gives your intelligence more depth and warmth.",
      advice: "In your next important conversation, count to three before answering and notice how often the other person adds something useful."
    },
    2: {
      text: "Your mind is focused on practical value. Mercury in the second house tends to think in terms of resources, earnings and what can be built, and you may have a sharp eye for a bargain or a gift for turning ideas into income. Writing, sales, bookkeeping, trading or teaching can all be profitable avenues. You tend to learn best when knowledge has a tangible use. The shadow is worrying constantly about money, or valuing ideas only for what they earn. Your sense of self-worth may also be linked to how clever you feel. Recognising that your mind is itself an asset helps you invest in skills that pay over time.",
      advice: "Keep a simple record of your income and spending for a month, and note which of your skills bring in the most value."
    },
    3: {
      text: "Mercury is at home here, and your mind is fast, curious and endlessly busy. The third house emphasises communication, learning and local connections, so you may be a natural writer, talker, teacher or networker. Siblings or neighbours often play a lively role in your life, and you tend to know what is going on around you before anyone else. Short trips, podcasts, puzzles and conversation keep you engaged. Scattered attention is the main hazard, along with gossip or never finishing what you start, and information overload can leave you anxious. Choosing what to focus on, and finishing one thing before starting the next, turns your quick mind into a real strength.",
      advice: "Limit yourself to three active projects at once, and finish or drop one before taking on anything new."
    },
    4: {
      text: "Your thinking is rooted in the past and the home. Mercury in the fourth house often means your family was talkative, bookish or full of strong opinions, and your early home shaped how you think. You may work from home, keep books and papers everywhere, or enjoy researching family history, local history or property. Your mind tends to process things privately before sharing. The trouble is getting stuck in old ways of thinking, or carrying family arguments into adulthood. As you grow older, your mind may become more active and reflective. A quiet, well-organised study or corner of the house can become the centre of your best thinking.",
      advice: "Set up one corner of your home as a dedicated thinking space, free of clutter and interruptions, for writing or planning."
    },
    5: {
      text: "Your mind loves to play. With Mercury in the fifth house, you tend to think creatively, enjoy games, puzzles and banter, and may express yourself through writing, performance or storytelling. Romance often begins with a good conversation, and you may be drawn to witty, clever partners. You can be a lively teacher or companion for children, able to explain things in a way that makes them laugh. The weak spot is treating serious matters too lightly, or needing an audience for your ideas. Speculating on hunches can also be risky. When you give your creative ideas some structure, they can become finished works you are proud of.",
      advice: "Pick one creative idea you keep talking about and give it a regular writing or making session until a draft exists."
    },
    6: {
      text: "You think best when you are solving practical problems. Mercury in the sixth house tends to give a precise, analytical mind that notices details others miss, and you are often good at organising, editing, troubleshooting or improving systems at work. You may enjoy learning about nutrition, fitness or daily habits. Colleagues often rely on your clear communication. The cost is worry, perfectionism or nervous tension, which can show up in the body as tightness or poor sleep, and you may criticise yourself harshly. Giving your mind useful work and then letting it rest, through walks, breathing or time with a pet, helps keep your nervous system calm.",
      advice: "End each workday by writing tomorrow's top three tasks, so your mind can stop rehearsing them once you leave."
    },
    7: {
      text: "Your mind comes alive in dialogue. With Mercury in the seventh house, you often think best when bouncing ideas off another person, and you may be drawn to partners who are clever, talkative or intellectually stimulating. You tend to be a good negotiator, mediator or consultant, able to see both sides of an argument. Contracts, agreements and paperwork may play a large role in your life. The difficulty is relying on others to make up your mind, or getting drawn into endless debates. Misunderstandings can be the main source of relationship stress. Clear agreements and honest conversation keep your partnerships healthy and your thinking your own.",
      advice: "Before signing any agreement or making a joint decision, write down your own view first so you know where you stand."
    },
    8: {
      text: "Your mind is drawn to secrets, psychology and what lies beneath. Mercury in the eighth house gives a probing, investigative intelligence, and you may be good at research, detective work, therapy, finance or anything that requires digging deep. You tend to notice what people leave unsaid, and conversations about sex, death, money or power do not scare you. The darker edge is suspicion, obsessive thinking or keeping your thoughts too private, and you may find it hard to speak about your own vulnerability. Writing or talking through difficult experiences can be transformative, turning painful knowledge into understanding that helps others as well as yourself.",
      advice: "When you catch yourself dwelling on a suspicion, write it down and look for evidence both for and against it."
    },
    9: {
      text: "Your mind reaches for the big picture. Mercury in the ninth house loves philosophy, foreign languages, travel, law and higher education, and you may be a natural teacher, writer or publisher. You tend to think in terms of meaning and principle, and you enjoy debating ideas with people from different backgrounds. Learning often continues throughout your life, long after formal study ends. The pitfall is becoming opinionated, preachy or impatient with details, and you may promise more than you can deliver when excited about a plan. Grounding your big ideas with facts and patient listening makes you a more convincing and generous communicator.",
      advice: "When sharing an opinion, back it with one concrete example and ask the other person for theirs before moving on."
    },
    10: {
      text: "Your voice and ideas are connected to your public role. With Mercury in the tenth house, you may be known for your communication skills, and careers in writing, media, teaching, sales, law or administration often suit you. You tend to plan your career carefully and think strategically about reputation. People may see you as clever or well informed. A parent may have been a strong influence on how you think or speak. The strain comes from overworking your mind or worrying about how your words are received, and you may change career direction several times. Speaking with authority about what you truly know builds a lasting reputation.",
      advice: "Choose one area of expertise and share your knowledge publicly, through a talk, article or post, at least once a quarter."
    },
    11: {
      text: "Your mind thrives in groups. Mercury in the eleventh house often makes you a lively networker, someone who connects people, shares information and brings fresh ideas to communities. You may be drawn to technology, science, social causes or online forums. Friends tend to be intellectually stimulating, and you may have many acquaintances across different circles. You think about the future and enjoy imagining how things could be better. Friendships can stay on a mental level, though, and you may talk about change more than you act on it. Your hopes gain traction when you turn ideas into plans with the people who share them.",
      advice: "Join or start a group focused on an idea you care about, and take on one concrete task within it."
    },
    12: {
      text: "Your mind works quietly, often below the surface. With Mercury in the twelfth house, you may think in images, feelings and intuitions more than straight lines, and your best ideas can arrive in dreams, meditation or solitude. You may find it hard to express yourself in public, yet write beautifully in private. Research, poetry, psychology, spiritual study and behind-the-scenes work suit you. The struggle is self-doubt, confusion or keeping important thoughts secret until they fester. Early experiences may have taught you to stay quiet. Journalling, therapy or creative writing can give your inner voice the space it needs to emerge.",
      advice: "Write freely for ten minutes each morning without editing, and look back weekly for ideas worth developing."
    }
  },

  venus: {
    1: {
      text: "Grace tends to arrive with you. Venus in the first house gives a pleasing manner and an eye for how things look, so your clothes, your posture and even the way you enter a conversation often carry a sense of style. People warm to you quickly, and you can smooth over awkward moments almost without trying. Your instinct is to approach life by cooperating and making things agreeable. The catch is that likeability can become a habit you hide behind: you may say yes to keep the peace, or feel uneasy whenever someone is displeased with you. Your charm lands best when it rests on honesty, including the occasional unwelcome truth.",
      advice: "Say one honest thing this week that you would usually soften to keep the peace, and notice how the relationship holds."
    },
    2: {
      text: "Pleasure and money are closely linked for you. With Venus in the second house, you have a feel for quality, and you would usually rather own one beautiful, well-made thing than ten cheap ones. Earning often comes more easily when your work involves beauty, food, design, music, fashion or making people comfortable, and your relaxed attitude to money can actually help attract it. Your self-worth tends to be fairly steady and rooted in your senses. On a bad day, though, you can spend to feel good, or mistake gifts and comforts for love. Knowing exactly what you value lets you enjoy wealth without being ruled by it.",
      advice: "Before a significant purchase, wait forty-eight hours and ask whether it reflects your values or just a passing mood."
    },
    3: {
      text: "Your words tend to carry warmth. Venus in the third house gives a gracious, persuasive way of speaking and writing, and you may have a good ear for language, rhythm or music. Everyday exchanges matter to you, so a kind message or a pleasant chat with a neighbour can lift your whole day. Siblings or cousins may be close friends, and romance sometimes begins somewhere ordinary, in a class, on a local walk or through a message thread. You learn best in agreeable company. The weak spot is tact that slides into flattery, or dodging difficult conversations to keep things sweet. Kindness and candour together make you genuinely convincing.",
      advice: "Write a thoughtful letter or message to a sibling or old friend, saying something appreciative you have never put into words."
    },
    4: {
      text: "Venus in the fourth house puts love at the heart of your private life. You tend to put real care into your home, from the colours on the walls to the food on the table, and guests often feel instantly at ease there. Family bonds can be affectionate, and you may carry fond memories of a parent who taught you to appreciate beauty or comfort. Property, interiors, gardens and hospitality can all be good fields for you, and the later years often bring a gentler, more contented life. The tension lies in keeping family peace at any cost, or polishing the surface while real feelings go unspoken. Warmth grows when honesty is welcome at home.",
      advice: "Invite friends or family into your home more often, and let the gathering be relaxed rather than perfectly arranged."
    },
    5: {
      text: "Romance, art and pleasure are strongly favoured here. With Venus in the fifth house, you tend to love the rituals of courtship, the thrill of attraction and the joy of making something beautiful. Creative gifts in music, drawing, fashion, performance or craft often come naturally, and you may have an easy rapport with children, who respond to your sense of fun. Affection flows freely from you, and you like to be adored in return. The risk is falling for the feeling of being in love more than the person, or chasing pleasure until it loses its sweetness. When delight is paired with some commitment, your romantic and creative life deepens.",
      advice: "Commit to one creative hobby for a full season, and notice how steady practice deepens the pleasure you take in it."
    },
    6: {
      text: "You bring grace to ordinary work. Venus in the sixth house tends to make you the colleague who smooths tensions, remembers how people take their tea and makes the office a nicer place to be. Your workplace needs to feel pleasant for you to do your best, and a tidy desk or a good playlist can change your whole output. Work in beauty, wellbeing, design or caring professions may suit you, and some people meet a partner through their job or through looking after animals. The shadow is avoiding the tedious parts of work, or leaning on sweet treats and comfort to get through the day. Gentle, enjoyable routines keep your body and mood in good tune.",
      advice: "Make your daily workspace a little more beautiful, and pair one unpleasant task each day with a small reward afterwards."
    },
    7: {
      text: "Partnership is one of the great themes of your life. With Venus in the seventh house, you tend to flourish in close one-to-one relationships and often attract partners who are attractive, cultured or kind. You have a natural sense of fairness, which makes you good at negotiation, mediation and business alliances as well as marriage. People tend to feel understood by you. The difficulty is keeping the peace so carefully that your own wishes disappear, or idealising a partner until reality disappoints. Some people with this placement feel incomplete when single. Your relationships thrive when you bring your own preferences and opinions to the table as openly as your affection.",
      advice: "Ask yourself what you want from a relationship before asking what your partner wants, and share both answers openly."
    },
    8: {
      text: "For you, love is serious and transformative. Venus in the eighth house seeks depth, loyalty and emotional honesty, and casual affairs rarely satisfy you for long. Intimacy, including sexual intimacy, can be a profound source of connection. You may benefit through a partner's resources, an inheritance or shared investments, and you might be drawn to work with other people's money or to therapeutic professions. There is often an ability to find beauty in grief and hard truths. The darker edge shows up as jealousy, possessiveness or bargaining with affection. Love here asks for trust, and when trust is present, relationships can change both of you for the better.",
      advice: "Have an open conversation with your partner about shared money and expectations before tensions build up around it."
    },
    9: {
      text: "Distance and difference tend to attract you. Venus in the ninth house often brings a love of travel, languages, foreign art and big ideas, and you may fall for someone from another country, culture or belief system. Beauty, for you, is tied to meaning: a moving piece of philosophy or a sunrise in an unfamiliar city can feel almost like romance. Teaching, publishing, travel or cross-cultural work may suit you well. You tend to be open-hearted and generous about other people's views. The pitfall is idealising what is far away while undervaluing the relationship in front of you. Shared adventures and learning keep your love life alive.",
      advice: "Plan a trip or class with your partner or a close friend that explores something new for both of you."
    },
    10: {
      text: "Charm is part of your professional reputation. With Venus in the tenth house, people often find you easy to work with, and you may rise through goodwill, taste and diplomacy as much as through effort. Careers in the arts, design, fashion, beauty, public relations or diplomacy can suit you, and you may be known for your style. Relationships and career sometimes overlap, through a partner met at work or a business shared with someone you love. A parent may have modelled grace or social ease. The risk is relying on likeability instead of building solid skill, or avoiding necessary conflict. Success feels best when your work expresses your values.",
      advice: "Identify one professional skill that complements your charm, and invest in developing it over the next six months."
    },
    11: {
      text: "Friendship carries a special sweetness for you. Venus in the eleventh house tends to bring warm, loyal friends and a talent for making groups feel welcoming, and you may be the one who organises the gathering or keeps the group chat kind. Some people with this placement find a partner among friends, or turn a partner into their best friend. Your hopes often involve beauty, harmony or fairness, and you may support artistic or social causes. The difficulty comes when you avoid friction in groups or keep friendships pleasant but shallow. Friends become lasting allies when you trust them with disagreement as well as affection.",
      advice: "Reach out to a friend you admire and suggest collaborating on something you both care about, whether creative or community-based."
    },
    12: {
      text: "Your capacity for love is deep, quiet and often private. With Venus in the twelfth house, you may love selflessly, feel drawn to secret or unconventional relationships, or find that some of your most tender feelings stay unspoken. Art, music, poetry and time alone in beautiful places can be deeply restorative, and you may feel a spiritual or compassionate calling. Work in charities, care settings or the arts suits your gentle side. The harder pattern is loving people who are unavailable, or giving so much that you disappear. Learning that you deserve the same kindness you offer others brings your love into the open.",
      advice: "Notice when you give more than you receive in a relationship, and ask clearly for one thing you need this week."
    }
  },

  mars: {
    1: {
      text: "Energy is your calling card. With Mars in the first house, you tend to meet life head on, move quickly and take the lead, and people sense your drive the moment you arrive. You are often brave, competitive and happiest when there is a challenge in front of you. Physical activity is usually essential, and you may have a strong build or a quick, decisive way of moving. Starting things comes easily; sustaining them can take more effort. The trouble is impatience, a short fuse or charging ahead before others are ready, which can come across as aggressive even when you mean well. Regular physical outlets help your courage stay constructive.",
      advice: "Build vigorous exercise into most days, and use the energy it gives you to tackle your hardest task first."
    },
    2: {
      text: "Mars in the second house puts real fire behind earning a living. You tend to be self-reliant, hardworking and fiercely independent about money, and you would usually rather earn it yourself than depend on anyone else. Trades, sport, business, physical work or anything that rewards initiative can suit you. You defend your values and your belongings with vigour. The trouble shows up as impulsive spending, rushing into risky ventures or rows over money, and you may measure your worth by how hard you work. Channelling your energy into long-term goals turns your drive into stable security, and your self-worth steadies when it rests on character as well as income.",
      advice: "Set one clear savings goal and automate regular transfers, so your drive to earn builds security instead of funding impulse purchases."
    },
    3: {
      text: "Your mind moves fast, and your words tend to be direct. Mars in the third house gives you a combative, energetic style of communication, and you may love debate, bold writing, sales or any work that requires quick thinking. You often say what others are only thinking. A sibling may have been a rival or a fierce ally, and early competition may have sharpened your wit. You tend to be restless locally, always walking, cycling or driving somewhere. The hazard is sharp words, heated arguments or haste on the road. Learning to pause before you reply turns your frankness into persuasive power, and people come to trust you for saying it straight.",
      advice: "When you feel the urge to argue, take a breath and ask a question first, then decide whether the point is worth making."
    },
    4: {
      text: "Your drive is focused on your home base. With Mars in the fourth house, you may throw yourself into renovations, gardening or moving house, and you tend to defend your family fiercely. Early home life may have been lively, crowded or conflict-ridden, and there may be strong feelings toward one parent. Anger can stay hidden in public, only to burst out at home among the people you are closest to. Restlessness in your living situation is common. The gift is a powerful instinct to protect and build a secure base. The challenge is learning to express frustration early and cleanly, so your home becomes a source of strength instead of tension.",
      advice: "Take on a physical home project, like gardening or renovation, when you feel frustration building, and let the work release it."
    },
    5: {
      text: "You pursue pleasure with passion. Mars in the fifth house brings energy to creativity, romance, sport and play, and you often enjoy a challenge, a competition or the chase of courtship. Creative work may be bold, physical or performative, and you may be drawn to drama, dance or competitive games. With children, you tend to be an active, lively presence who is happy to join the rough and tumble. Romance can be exciting and occasionally stormy. The risk is taking chances for the thrill, whether with money, love or safety, and becoming too competitive to enjoy the fun. When your fire goes into creative projects and physical play, it becomes a real source of joy.",
      advice: "Channel your competitive energy into a sport or creative challenge with clear rules, so the thrill has a healthy outlet."
    },
    6: {
      text: "Work is where your energy pours out. Mars in the sixth house tends to make you productive, efficient and impatient with slackness, and you often do best in jobs that are physical, fast-paced or focused on fixing problems. Fitness, trades, emergency services and technical work may appeal. Colleagues may see you as a driving force, and you may clash with those who work more slowly. Your body often needs daily exercise to stay balanced. The downside is overwork, irritability or ignoring early signs of strain until you are exhausted. Pacing yourself, and dealing with workplace frustrations directly, keeps your energy strong for the long run.",
      advice: "Build short movement breaks into your workday, and address small workplace frictions early before they become open conflict."
    },
    7: {
      text: "Relationships bring out your fire. With Mars in the seventh house, you may attract strong, assertive or passionate partners, and your closest bonds tend to be lively, challenging and rarely dull. You often fight hard for fairness and can be a powerful advocate for others. Partnerships may spark growth through friction, and a good argument can feel strangely intimate. The trouble is conflict, power struggles or projecting your own anger onto a partner, so that you seem to keep meeting aggressive people. Open rivals or legal disputes may appear in your life. Owning your assertiveness, and voicing it yourself, brings balance to your closest relationships.",
      advice: "When you feel irritated with a partner, ask yourself what you want that you have not yet asked for directly."
    },
    8: {
      text: "Your will is deep, intense and hard to deflect. Mars in the eighth house gives strong desire, sexual energy and the courage to face what others avoid. You may be drawn to crisis work, surgery, research, investigation or finance, and you tend to stay calm when things fall apart. Shared money, debt or inheritance can become a battleground or a project you tackle with determination. When you want something, you pursue it with total focus. The darker side is jealousy, control or anger that simmers until it erupts. Honest intimacy and a worthwhile challenge give your intensity somewhere good to go, and your resilience can be remarkable.",
      advice: "When anger surfaces in close relationships, name it early and calmly, before it builds into a power struggle."
    },
    9: {
      text: "Belief gives you energy. Mars in the ninth house tends to make you a crusader for your ideas, eager to explore, debate and act on what you think is right. You may love adventurous travel, outdoor pursuits, study or activism, and you can be an inspiring teacher or advocate. Law, politics, publishing and sport can all appeal. You often move quickly when a cause grips you. The risk is dogmatism, arguing too hard or treating disagreement as a fight to win. You may also take unnecessary risks while travelling. Your conviction becomes persuasive when it is matched by genuine curiosity about other views.",
      advice: "Before debating a belief, study the strongest argument for the other side so your own case stands on firm ground."
    },
    10: {
      text: "Ambition burns strongly here. With Mars in the tenth house, you tend to want to lead, achieve and be recognised for what you have done, and you often seek careers that reward initiative, courage or competition. Business, the military, sport, surgery, engineering or self-employment can suit you. A parent may have been forceful or demanding, shaping your drive. You may be seen as bold or pioneering, and you rarely wait for permission. The difficulty is clashing with authority, burning out or making enemies through impatience. Pursuing goals that truly matter to you, and learning to collaborate, turns your drive into lasting achievement.",
      advice: "Choose one long-term career goal and break it into small, achievable steps, celebrating each one to keep your drive steady."
    },
    11: {
      text: "You put your energy behind the future you want. Mars in the eleventh house tends to make you an active force in groups, whether in activism, team sports, community projects or professional networks. You often rally people around a cause and push for change. Friends may be energetic, competitive or strong-willed, and you enjoy doing things together more than just talking. The hazard is clashing with others in the group, forcing your views or falling out with friends over principles. Learning to share leadership, and choosing causes worth your fire, lets you make a real difference.",
      advice: "Pick one cause you care about and volunteer regular, concrete time to it, working alongside others rather than alone."
    },
    12: {
      text: "Your drive tends to work below the surface. With Mars in the twelfth house, you may find it hard to assert yourself openly or even recognise when you are angry, and frustration can leak out sideways as tiredness, passive resistance or self-sabotage. Yet you may also have great energy for hidden work, research, spiritual practice or fighting on behalf of those who cannot defend themselves. Solitary exercise such as swimming or long runs can be powerfully restoring. The challenge is learning to feel and express anger safely before it turns inward. When you do, you gain a quiet, steady strength that others often underestimate.",
      advice: "Find a private physical outlet, like swimming or running alone, where you can release built-up tension without an audience."
    }
  },

  jupiter: {
    1: {
      text: "Jupiter in the first house tends to give a warm, expansive presence. People often see you as generous, optimistic and larger than life, and your enthusiasm can lift a room. You approach life with faith that things will work out, and doors often seem to open for you. You may be a natural teacher, motivator or storyteller. Your body may carry weight easily or have a broad, robust quality. The difficulty is overconfidence, overcommitting or indulging too freely in food, spending or promises. Grounding your optimism in realistic plans, and sharing your luck with others, turns natural good fortune into genuine wisdom.",
      advice: "Before committing to a new venture, write down realistic costs and time, then decide whether your enthusiasm still holds."
    },
    2: {
      text: "Abundance often gathers around your resources. With Jupiter in the second house, you tend to have a generous, hopeful attitude toward money, and opportunities to earn may arrive through teaching, publishing, law, travel or any field that widens horizons. Your talents can be broad, and you usually appreciate quality and learning. You enjoy sharing what you have. The pitfall is extravagance, overspending or assuming more will always come, which can leave you stretched. Your self-worth may be tied to how generous you can be. Balancing openhandedness with some planning helps your wealth grow steadily, and seeing your character as your greatest asset keeps your values clear.",
      advice: "Set aside a fixed percentage of every payment for savings before spending, so abundance builds up rather than slipping away."
    },
    3: {
      text: "Curiosity knows few limits for you. Jupiter in the third house brings a love of reading, writing, learning and conversation, and you may be a gifted communicator, teacher or storyteller. You tend to see connections and the bigger picture, and people enjoy your enthusiasm for ideas. Relationships with siblings or neighbours are often supportive, and short trips may bring luck or opportunity. You may pick up languages or new subjects with ease. The difficulty is exaggerating, talking too much or skimming details, and starting courses you never finish is common. Focusing your curiosity on fewer subjects lets your knowledge grow deep as well as wide.",
      advice: "Choose one subject to study in depth this year, and teach what you learn to someone else as you go."
    },
    4: {
      text: "Home and family tend to be sources of blessing for you. Jupiter in the fourth house often indicates a generous or expansive upbringing, or a family with strong values, faith or cultural traditions. You may want a spacious home, enjoy hosting and feel happiest when your door is open to others. Property can be a rewarding area of life, and your later years often bring comfort and a sense of fulfilment. The difficulty is overindulgence at home, restlessness about where you live or taking family support for granted. A home that nurtures growth and welcomes others becomes the foundation for everything else you do.",
      advice: "Open your home regularly to others, whether through hosting meals or gatherings, and let generosity make your space feel fuller."
    },
    5: {
      text: "Joy comes naturally with Jupiter in the fifth house. You tend to be playful, generous and expressive, and creative projects, romance and fun can bring luck and growth. You may have a gift for performance, art or teaching, and children often bring you great happiness, whether your own or those you mentor. Romance can be exciting and plentiful. The risk is overdoing it: gambling, overspending on pleasure or chasing romance for its own sake. You may also find it hard to take your creativity seriously enough to finish what you start. Sharing your gifts generously and nurturing young people's talents often brings deep satisfaction.",
      advice: "Share your creative gifts generously, perhaps by teaching or mentoring a young person in something you love."
    },
    6: {
      text: "Meaning often arrives through work. Jupiter in the sixth house tends to bring good working conditions, supportive colleagues and opportunities to grow on the job, and you may thrive in education, service or caring roles. You tend to be generous with colleagues and enjoy helping others improve. Daily habits can support your wellbeing, and you may take a lively interest in food, exercise or holistic living. Animals may be a source of joy. The trouble is overcommitting, saying yes to every extra task or overindulging in food and comfort. Balancing ambition with rest keeps your optimism steady and your body strong.",
      advice: "Review your commitments monthly and drop at least one task that no longer serves you, protecting time for rest."
    },
    7: {
      text: "Partnership tends to bring growth and good fortune. With Jupiter in the seventh house, you may attract generous, wise or successful partners, and marriage or business alliances can open doors for you. You tend to be fair, optimistic and supportive in relationships, and people often seek your counsel. Agreements and contracts often work in your favour. The difficulty is idealising partners, expecting them to provide meaning or overlooking warning signs. Some people with this placement marry more than once or choose partners from different cultures. Choosing partners who share your values, and growing alongside them, helps your relationships flourish over the long term.",
      advice: "Discuss your long-term dreams openly with your partner, and look for practical ways to support each other's growth."
    },
    8: {
      text: "Jupiter in the eighth house tends to bring abundance through shared resources, inheritance, investments or a partner's income. You may work in finance, insurance, research or therapy, and you often have deep psychological insight. Crises can bring unexpected growth, and you may recover from loss more fully than you expected. Intimacy can be generous and transformative. The difficulty is excess: overspending shared money, taking on debt or chasing intense experiences. You may also use optimism to avoid darker emotions. Honest dealings with shared resources, and using your insight to help others heal, bring lasting growth.",
      advice: "Review joint finances or debts regularly with your partner, keeping generosity and caution in balance."
    },
    9: {
      text: "Jupiter is at home in the ninth house, and you tend to be a natural seeker of meaning. Travel, higher education, philosophy, law and spirituality often bring growth and good fortune, and you may inspire others with your vision. Foreign cultures may feel like home, and you may live or study abroad. Teaching, publishing, law or religion can be natural fields. The difficulty is dogmatism, restlessness or overpromising, and you may neglect practical matters in pursuit of big ideas. Grounding your wisdom in lived experience, and sharing it with humility, makes you a genuinely inspiring teacher or guide.",
      advice: "Plan one trip or course each year that challenges your beliefs, then share what you learned with others."
    },
    10: {
      text: "Recognition often comes to you through your career. Jupiter in the tenth house tends to bring success, authority and a good reputation, and others often see you as capable, trustworthy and generous. You may work in law, education, politics, publishing or any field that widens horizons. A parent may have been generous, influential or a model of success. The difficulty is overambition, arrogance or taking on more responsibility than you can handle, and you may lean too heavily on luck. Using your position to help others, and staying humble, keeps your reputation strong and your success meaningful.",
      advice: "Mentor someone earlier in their career, sharing your experience generously as a way of honouring the support you received."
    },
    11: {
      text: "Friends and networks tend to be a source of good fortune for you. Jupiter in the eleventh house often brings many friends, supportive communities and generous groups, and you may be involved in causes that make a real difference. Your hopes are often big and optimistic, and friends may help you realise them. You tend to be a generous friend yourself, quick to make introductions. The difficulty is overcommitting to groups, relying too much on others or spreading yourself thin across too many circles. You may also idealise friends. Choosing a few meaningful causes and nurturing close friendships helps your hopes come true.",
      advice: "Pick one group or cause that aligns with your values and commit to it fully, rather than spreading yourself thin."
    },
    12: {
      text: "Hidden blessings tend to follow you. Jupiter in the twelfth house often brings spiritual depth, compassion and a sense of protection in hard times, and you may feel guided even when you cannot explain why. Solitude, meditation and retreat can bring deep peace. You may work in hospitals, charities or spiritual settings, and your kindness often goes unseen. The difficulty is escapism, excess or self-sacrifice, and you may hide your gifts or let others take advantage of your generosity. Nurturing your inner life, and letting your compassion be seen, brings fulfilment and allows your quiet wisdom to help others.",
      advice: "Set aside regular time for quiet reflection or volunteering, letting generosity flow from a well-rested and grounded place."
    }
  }
};
